# Moddy Arena: the prep phase and a battle's wishes. In prep, an Apprentice make from the prep room lands in the arena
# ahead of him and one made standing in the arena lands there; a recipe wish (the starter Lightning Sword, made again
# by its recipe) is put on his hotbar from its page in My wishes. In the battle the hotbar makes it again with one
# click, a second click at once is refused with the seconds left, and a new make is refused with the arena's words.
# After the battle the wish is still on his hotbar and new makes work again. No model anywhere: the Apprentice's local
# matcher offers the makes, and the hotbar replays a kept recipe.
@intent in prep a player makes things from the prep room and in the arena and puts a recipe wish on his hotbar; in a battle the hotbar fires it, it rests between fires, and new wishes are refused; after the battle the hotbar wish is still there
@world flat seed=1
@continue-on-fail

@step arrive
@expect chat Welcome to Moddy Arena within 90s
@expect chat add them to your hotbar within 10s
@wait 2s
difficulty hard
difficulty normal
effect give @s minecraft:resistance 900 4 true
effect give @s minecraft:saturation 900 0 true

@step what the arena says about wishes in prep
moddy wishes
@expect chat Magician wishes left before the next battle: 3 of 3 within 5s
@expect chat Builder and Apprentice wishes are free within 5s

@step a make from the prep room lands in the arena ahead of him
# the core's Builder puts a make 12 blocks ahead of him: from the middle of the prep room, facing the arena, that is
# through the gate on the arena's floor
tp @s 0.5 64 21.5 180 0
@aim look 180 12
@wait 2s
moddy apprentice a stone well
@expect screen Container within 10s
@shot prep-room-apprentice-page
@click slot 0
@expect chat /is ready/ within 90s
@wait 3s
# the arena ahead of the gate is no longer empty air (compared with the empty sky at y 200): the well stands in it
@assert execute unless blocks -4 64 3 4 67 15 -4 200 3 all
@shot made-from-the-prep-room

@step a recipe wish in the prep room: the starter Lightning Sword
moddy again starter_lightning_sword
@expect chat /[Ll]ightning [Ss]word/ within 60s
@wait 3s
@shot the-sword

@step a make in the arena lands there
tp @s 0 64 10 180 0
@aim look 180 12
@wait 2s
moddy apprentice a cozy house
@expect screen Container within 10s
@click slot 0
@expect chat /is ready/ within 90s
@wait 3s
@assert execute unless blocks -15 64 -15 15 67 3 -15 200 -15 all
@shot made-in-the-arena

@step the Lightning Sword wish goes on his hotbar
# In a real game: My wishes, RIGHT-click the Lightning Sword's tile (a left click makes another one), "Add to hotbar".
# The carrier clicks with the left button only, so this script makes another one with the left click (a kept thing made
# again, which the arena lets through), and then puts the proxy where "Add to hotbar" puts it, with the data the core
# writes (the recipe, its owner, its picture): the core's own use of it is what the battle below exercises.
moddy library
@expect screen My wishes within 10s
@shot my-wishes
@click item "lightning"
@expect chat /Lightning Sword is in slot/ within 30s
@wait 1s
item replace entity @s hotbar.3 with minecraft:paper[custom_data={mfam_hotbar:"starter_lightning_sword",mfam_hotbar_owner:"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",mfam_hotbar_icon:"minecraft:diamond_sword"},custom_name="Wish: Lightning Sword",max_stack_size=1]
@assert execute if items entity @s hotbar.3 minecraft:paper
@shot on-the-hotbar

@step he starts a battle with the button
tp @s 1.5 64 19.5 180 0
@wait 1s
@aim pos 2.5 65.5 17.1
@key key.use
@expect chat A battle is starting within 5s
moddy wishes
@expect chat fire your wishes from your hotbar within 5s

@step wave 1, and the hotbar makes the sword again
@expect title Wave 1 of 5 within 15s
tp @s 0 64 10 180 0
@aim look 180 30
@wait 1s
@assert execute if entity @e[tag=moddyarena_wave]
@assert execute if items entity @s hotbar.3 minecraft:paper
@key key.hotbar.4
@wait 5t
@assert execute if items entity @s weapon.mainhand minecraft:paper
@key key.use
@expect chat /[Ll]ightning [Ss]word/ within 60s
@shot fired-from-the-hotbar

@step at once again: it rests, and says how long
# past the core's own one-second sweep, well inside the arena's ten-second rest
@wait 2s
@key key.use
@expect actionbar /That wish is resting. It is ready again in [0-9]+ seconds?/ within 5s
@shot resting

@step a new make in the battle is refused
moddy apprentice a cozy house
@expect screen Container within 10s
@click slot 0
@expect chat only the wishes on your hotbar work now within 10s
@wait 2s
@shot new-wish-refused

@step the battle is won
kill @e[tag=moddyarena_wave]
@expect chat Wave 1 cleared within 5s
@expect title Wave 2 of 5 within 20s
@wait 1s
kill @e[tag=moddyarena_wave]
@expect title Wave 3 of 5 within 20s
@wait 1s
kill @e[tag=moddyarena_wave]
@expect title Wave 4 of 5 within 20s
@wait 1s
kill @e[tag=moddyarena_wave]
@expect title Wave 5 of 5 within 20s
@wait 1s
kill @e[tag=moddyarena_wave]
@expect chat You won the battle within 5s
@expect chat The arena is tidy again within 15s

@step after the battle the hotbar wish is still there, and new makes work again
@assert execute if items entity @s hotbar.3 minecraft:paper
moddy wishes
@expect chat Magician wishes left before the next battle: 3 of 3 within 5s
tp @s 0 64 10 180 0
@aim look 180 12
@wait 2s
moddy apprentice a cozy house
@expect screen Container within 10s
@click slot 0
@expect chat /is ready/ within 90s
@wait 2s
@shot after-the-battle

@step knocked out: what happens to a hotbar wish (the core's own rule)
kill @s
@wait 3s
@shot after-knocked-out
# back in the prep room: the hotbar wish is not in his inventory, and was not dropped either
@assert execute if entity @s[x=-4,y=63,z=17,dx=8,dy=3,dz=8]
@assert execute unless items entity @s container.* minecraft:paper
@assert execute unless entity @e[type=minecraft:item,nbt={Item:{id:"minecraft:paper"}}]
